<title>TURKEY: Turk Cukurova Elektrik H1 profit down.</title>
<headline>Turk Cukurova Elektrik H1 profit down.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit(lira) 11,978.84  vs   5,670.34</p>
<p>    Net profit		  5,989.42  vs   2,835.17</p>
<p>    Net sales		  22,123.48  vs  11,830.12</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  7,435.16  vs   5,877.35</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	3,328.61  vs     660.87</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     2,853.06  vs   2,079.82</p>
<p>    Total debts		29,640.84  vs  18,686.19</p>
<p>    Equity		     10,896.18  vs   4,869.07</p>
<p>    Capital			 500.00  vs     500.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Cukurova Elektrik A.S is Turkey's biggest private sector utility controlled by the Rumeli group. It produces and distributies electricty in southern Cukurova region.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
